    "VISUAL_NAME": "Grid",
    "SCHEMA_NAME": "FAM_ASSET_VERIFICATION_COVERAGE",
    "SCHEMA_DESCR": "Asset Verification Coverage by Category. For each asset category, shows TOTAL_ASSETS = count of in-service assets (FAM_ASSET_REGISTER.STATUS='ACTIVE', grounded via distinct_values against the live DB which returned ACTIVE/DISPOSED/DRAFT/UNDER_MAINTENANCE - ACTIVE is the in-service/capitalized state, DRAFT/UNDER_MAINTENANCE/DISPOSED are excluded), VERIFIED_ASSETS = count of those same in-service assets that have at least one FAM_PHYSICAL_VERIFICATION_LINE row with a non-null VERIFIED_DATE falling inside the selected period (the verification LINE's own VERIFIED_DATE is used, not FAM_ASSET_REGISTER.LAST_VERIFIED_DATE, so the % reflects verification events that actually happened within the chosen window), and PCT_VERIFIED = VERIFIED_ASSETS/TOTAL_ASSETS*100 (0 when TOTAL_ASSETS is 0, guarded via CASE). PERIOD CRITERION: implemented as a single editable 'Verification Period From' date prompt (Criteria_2, real column FAM_PHYSICAL_VERIFICATION_LINE.VERIFIED_DATE, operator >=, default 12 months before today = 2025-08-11) paired with an implicit upper bound of CURRENT_DATE baked into SOURCE_SQL - this project had no existing months-back numeric or from/to date-range convention to reuse (checked all sibling visual_models), so a single FROM-date prompt was chosen as the closest fit to the project's one existing rolling-date pattern (fam_depreciation_comparison_ca_it's single 'As On Date' prompt), letting the user pick how far back the verification window starts while always ending 'today'. CATEGORY CRITERION: optional CATEGORY_CODE filter (Criteria_1, like + '%' default + lookup to FAM_ASSET_CATEGORY_MASTER) - left blank shows all categories.",
    "SCHEMA_TYPE": "S",
    "OUTPUT_TYPE": "JSON",
    "DATABASE_TYPE": "1",
    "DATABASE_DETAIL": { "DATABASE_NAME": "PostgreSQL", "TYPE": 1 }
